! NOTE: HYDROPONIC SOLUTION section is an APPROXIMATION added 2026-08-04. The
!       real UFGA2402 experiment (Coon dissertation, Ch. 3/4, AEC model source
!       for the 21/25/31/34C treatments) was NOT hydroponic NFT: it was
!       1-gallon pots of soilless substrate (Pro-Mix HP Mycorrhizae) with
!       slow-release Osmocote Plus 15N-9P2O5-12K2O fertilizer, watered to
!       field capacity, not fed liquid nutrient solution. This HS section is
!       a hydroponic-equivalent-feed stand-in, not a literature setpoint.
! NOTE: KC corrected 99.6 (was 250.0, an apparent copy-paste from UFGA2201's
!       generic recipe). Derived from Osmocote's guaranteed analysis: K2O 12%
!       -> elemental K 12%*(2*39.098/94.196)=9.96%; P2O5 9% -> elemental P
!       9%*(2*30.974/141.944)=3.93%. Applying the fertilizer's N:P:K mass
!       ratio (15:3.93:9.96) to the existing NO3C=150 gives P=39.3 (matches
!       file's PC=40.0 already, so PC left unchanged) and K=150*9.96/15=99.6.
!       NO3C/PC/CAC/MGC/SC absolute levels, and the Osmocote application rate
!       itself (dissertation states "6.26 g/m3", physically implausible for a
!       1-gal pot -- likely a kg/m3 typo -- so no absolute mg/L conversion was
!       attempted), remain UNVERIFIED approximations, not literature values.

